<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>

<chapter xml:id="ch-03-the-kitchen" xmlns:xi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XInclude">
  <title>The Kitchen</title>

  <introduction>
    <p>
      In the first two chapters, we have been focusing on the basic chemical structures of household products.
      Now we move to the kitchen, where exciting chemistry happens with the same structures.
      Indeed, a major theme in this chapter is that molecules change their structure under certain conditions.
      These changes are called chemical reactions, and they drive everything in the kitchen.
    </p>
  </introduction>

